# Changes to the source of truth and to project governance require
# review by a code owner. See CLAUDE.md -> Working in this repository.
#
# Two owners, so neither ever has to approve their own pull request.
# GitHub does not permit a PR author to approve their own PR, so a
# single-owner file would deadlock every change to these paths.

/SKILL.md       @rsedilla @raneenicole
/README.md      @rsedilla @raneenicole
/docs/          @rsedilla @raneenicole
/.claude/       @rsedilla @raneenicole
/.github/       @rsedilla @raneenicole

# Agent instruction files are deliberately NOT anchored to the repository root.
# A leading slash matches only the root file, so `web/CLAUDE.md` -- which every
# agent working in `web/` reads -- would merge with neither owner seeing it. The
# risk is the file's standing rather than today's contents: it is a surface
# somebody eventually appends a project rule to, and that rule would land
# unreviewed in a repository whose governance rests on these files being read.
#
# Unanchored, so they cover an app directory before it exists. `AGENTS.md` is
# listed although no root one exists yet, for the same reason.
CLAUDE.md       @rsedilla @raneenicole
AGENTS.md       @rsedilla @raneenicole

# Migrations carry the constraints SKILL.md guarantees, and touch the history it
# says is preserved. They are reviewed on the same terms as the specification.
/api/migrations/            @rsedilla @raneenicole
